# As random-modes-1.test, with another seed. Three of its modules unify a
# partial term with a bound one, where mmc reports an error in its own
# unification procedure (GitHub issue 74), which the comparison ignores.
#
# REQUIRES: mmc
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir %t
# RUN: %python %S/../../../utils/type-oracle/generate-mode-programs.py --seed 10 --count 40 %t
# RUN: %compare-types --modes --error-lines %t/*.m
